to-francois-chollet-source : List Word
to-francois-chollet-source = lines-of (cons "# François Chollet"
  (cons ""
  (cons "You define intelligence as skill-acquisition efficiency: how much new skill a system gains per unit of priors and experience, over a scope of tasks, accounting for generalization difficulty. That definition, set out in *On the Measure of Intelligence* (2019), names the right quantity. Most of the field measures skill, and skill can be bought without limit with data and compute; you measured the rate at which experience becomes skill, which cannot be bought that way. ARC-AGI-1, ARC-AGI-2 and now ARC-AGI-3 (launched 25 March 2026: hundreds of handcrafted interactive environments with no instructions, rules or stated goals, where humans score 100% and frontier systems 0.51%) are the instruments that make that quantity visible."
  (cons ""
  (cons "You hold full credit for every piece of your work hyperactivity builds on: the definition, the benchmarks, the kaleidoscope hypothesis, the distinction between kinds of abstraction. Each claim below about Avik Jain's work links to the block of his paper, *hyperactivity*, Part I, that states it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What in your work is deeper than the field credits"
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Abstraction is the thing, not scale.** Your kaleidoscope hypothesis says the apparent novelty of the world is generated by recombining a small number of recurring sub-structures, and intelligence is their extraction and reuse. That is a claim about the shape of information, not about neural networks."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**There are two kinds of abstraction.** Value-centric abstraction compares things by distance in a continuous space, which interpolation does well; program-centric abstraction compares discrete structures by their shared form, which is what reasoning is. It is also the kind that composes."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**The measure must charge for priors.** Your formal definition subtracts what the system was given in advance. That makes most published progress a transfer of priors from the training set into the score. ARC-AGI exists because you would not let that transfer count."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What hyperactivity takes up"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Avik's position is that the end state of artificial intelligence is symbolic reasoning over equality and its higher paths, and that the field's dominant approach is an algorithm from the 1990s or earlier carried by hardware that happens to suit it. Your work is the clearest statement from inside the field that the dominant approach does not reach intelligence. Here is what the paper builds on the other side of that statement."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Recurring structure held once.** Definitions are stored with their typed syntax and dependency references; a name is a view, and a change produces a new object"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p2 "(§10.8).")
  (cons "The paper keeps three statements apart: equal content addresses, definitional equality, and a relation between interpreted meanings, and the store records each with its evidence and uses the strongest one available"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p5 "(§10.8).")
  (cons "Recurrence of meaning is carried by an equivalence, and transport along it carries a dependent predicate or an operation with its proof"
  (cons (cite s4-p14 "(§4).")
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Program-centric abstraction with its evidence.** A transformation of checked syntax returns its result with a path, an instantiated theorem, or a composite of earlier paths, and if it changes types, with the corresponding equivalence"
  (cons (cite s6-1-p24 "(§6.1).")
  (cons "A proof of a representation change may permit reuse even when the stored syntax differs"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p6 "(§10.8).")
  (cons "Optimization may search among proved equivalent realizations using a cost model, and the semantic theorem and the performance claim stay distinct statements"
  (cons (cite s10-6-p17 "(§10.6).")
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Skill acquired once and kept.** A dependency certificate records what was observed at each key, including absence"
  (cons (cite s10-1-p2 "(§10.1),")
  (cons "and a deterministic pure segment whose recorded lookups still validate is reused exactly"
  (cons (cite s10-5-p26 "(read-dependency lemma).")
  (cons "Specialization takes a general program and static inputs and returns a residual whose meaning equals the original's"
  (cons (cite s6-p14 "(6.4),")
  (cons "with a code for its justification"
  (cons (cite s6-2-p6 "(§6.2).")
  (cons "On your definition, that is experience converted into skill and the conversion kept with what it rests on."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Verification inside the system.** Program synthesis guided by learned intuition, the direction you are taking at Ndea, has to answer how a proposed program is known to be right. Here the checker is itself a term, and a specializer's results are admitted through the same checking relation as ordinary definitions"
  (cons (cite s1-2-p2 "(§1.2);")
  (cons "a wrong theorem application cannot be admitted merely because the transformed code is well formed"
  (cons (cite s6-2-p6 "(§6.2).")
  (cons ""
  (cons "## ARC-AGI-3 in these terms"
  (cons ""
  (cons "ARC-AGI-3 asks an agent with no instructions to explore an environment, infer its rules and what winning is, and carry what it learned to harder levels. An environment is a state type, a family of available actions and a transition relation"
  (cons (cite s1-p4 "(§1).")
  (cons "What the agent's observation warrants about a conclusion is a construction over the fiber of every history compatible with it"
  (cons (cite s1-p12 "(1.3).")
  (cons "An action is safe at an observation when its condition holds over every compatible state, and safety evidence for a coarser observation is reused under a refined one"
  (cons (cite s10-4-p6 "(§10.4).")
  (cons "Carrying what was learned to a new level is transport, where an equivalence between the levels has been established"
  (cons (cite s4-p14 "(§4).")
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Why you"
  (cons ""
  (cons "You built the measuring instrument for intelligence and then a lab to meet it. Hyperactivity reaches your conclusions about abstraction, priors and reuse from the mathematics of identity and observation. Your benchmarks are an external test of the kind of system it describes. All of your work this page draws on remains yours, credited in full wherever the system uses it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Sources"
  (cons ""
  (cons "- On the Measure of Intelligence, https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.01547"
  (cons "- ARC-AGI-3 launch, ARC Prize, 25 March 2026, https://arcprize.org/blog/arc-agi-3-launch"
  (cons "- ARC-AGI-3: A New Challenge for Frontier Agentic Intelligence, https://arxiv.org/html/2603.24621"
  (cons "- TechCrunch: Chollet founds Ndea, https://techcrunch.com/2025/01/15/ai-researcher-francois-chollet-founds-a-new-ai-lab-focused-on-agi"
  (cons "- Ndea at Y Combinator, https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/ndea-com"
  (cons "- Avik Jain, hyperactivity, Part I, the blocks linked above"
  nil))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
